{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790423093,"nonce":"LcTcn8GWjTwMOwAyAoyu/gPnMGk=","title":"Recompile only a cold loop's region","message":"When a loop compiled before it ran (a cold loop) starts running, recompile_top_tier compiles the whole function again (~9 ms for method_call's module body before f7cf6c1, loop 2 waiting in generic calls at ~17 ns/call). An OSR-only body for the region the cold header reaches would compile a fraction of that. The installed normal entry stays the old body; only the OSR table at that header moves. Part of 990178a.","files":null}]}